            Bag size makes Clean Simple Eats more expensive still. The brand also sells a 20-serving bag at $49.99 and a 10-serving bag at $29.99, which work out to about $3.12 and $3.75 per 25 g. Levels' 5 lb tub is the cheapest way to buy it; Vitacost also listed a 907 g size at $57.99, which by weight should hold about 28 servings, or roughly $2.13 per 25 g. We did not confirm that serving count on a label.
