        <div id="testing" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            7. Which Is Third-Party Tested, Clean Simple Eats or Levels?
          </h2>

          <p>
            Neither has a third-party certification we could verify. We did not find either brand in the NSF Certified for Sport database, and neither label carries an Informed Sport, Informed Choice or NSF mark. If you are a drug-tested athlete, that rules out both.
          </p>

          <p>
            Clean Simple Eats says its products are "3rd party tested," and our review found retailer listings describing testing for pathogens, heavy metals and gluten. But the brand does not name the lab or certifier, and it does not publish results on the product page. A brand statement like that is worth something, but less than a certification you can look up in a registry or a lab report you can read for yourself.
          </p>

          <p>
            Levels' Vitacost listing mentions a Clean Label Project Purity Award. We could not confirm a current, product-specific Clean Label Project certification for Levels Grass-Fed Whey, so we have not counted it. With the brand's own website parked when we checked, there was also nowhere to look for a test result from Levels directly.
          </p>

          <div class="bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-6 lg:p-8 my-8">
            <p class="text-xs font-black uppercase tracking-widest text-[#38BDF8] mb-3">IF TESTING MATTERS</p>
            <p class="text-xl font-bold text-white mb-3">Neither brand clears the bar for drug-tested athletes.</p>
            <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed m-0">Certification is granted product by product, and neither of these powders showed up in the registries we checked. If you need one, start with our <a href='/best-nsf-certified-protein-powder/'>NSF certified protein powder</a> guide; if your worry is contaminants rather than banned substances, see <a href='/best-protein-powder-without-heavy-metals/'>protein powder without heavy metals</a> and <a href='/is-protein-powder-safe/'>is protein powder safe</a>.</p>
          </div>
